  is the safest state as the ongoing  conflict makes it too risky to operate  international aid is finally trickling  into pakistan's flood-ravaged regions  today two more u.s military planes  arrived loaded with 35 tons of food and  first aid supplies months of deadly  monsoon rain has destroyed homes washed  away an entire year's crops and made  clean drinking water scarce the floods  have killed almost 1400 people it's  estimated 33 million more are now  displaced and dealing with hunger and  rising risk of water-borne diseases  and in the u.s poignant ceremonies were  held today as americans marched 21 years  since the 9 11 attacks  21 years ago  21 years and we still kept our promise  never forget  [Music]  president joe biden speaking at the  pentagon where one of the hijacked  planes killed nearly 200 people that day  of course there were also ceremonies in  new york to honor the victims of the  devastating world trade center attacks  nearly 3 000 people died in the terror  attacks in 2001.  next arriving directly from the palace  canada's high commissioner to the uk  discusses his meeting with the king  today we're back to london with donna  right after this short break  you're watching global national  welcome back to london canada's prime  minister the governor general and the  high commissioner to the uk ralph  goodale are invited to the queen's  funeral on september 19th there may be  others too the final guest list is still  being worked on i met mr goodell earlier  today on his way from meeting the new  king along with representatives from  other commonwealth countries  you've just come back from the palace  you met the new king for the first time  what was that like  well there was a  profound sense of history in the room so  the the king was there and the queen  consort  this event has never happened in the  last 70 years  one era turning to another era  a dominant personality much loved  in in queen elizabeth is gone  a new king has taken over so history is  changing and being a part of that change  of history  was one of the emotions in the room  another obviously was  was grief and mourning for  for queen elizabeth this is a big burden  for the new king charles to take on he's  lost his mother he's also taking on this  huge role  as you say from a woman who was so much  loved had so much respect  what sense did you get from him  personally today it's very personal he  has lost his mother anybody who's gone  through that experience knows how tough  that that is  you  you feel a bit orphaned  and of course he's lost both of his  parents in the course of the last year  and a bit yeah  so  it's got to be  unsettling disorienting and still  in the grieving process  he has to do it very much in public uh  the pressures  uh have to be enormous the stresses and  the strains  uh but  he certainly leaves you with the  impression that he is he is ready for  the job we talked a lot about uh  his recent visit to to canada he was  there in the spring a very busy agenda  and uh there were many components to it  but two in particular his connection  with the ukrainian diaspora in in canada  at this critical time and his  connections many of them uh with uh  indigenous communities  and  clearly there  uh i think he he he has a very real  sense of how important  truth reconciliation and healing is to  the future of canada  and  the role of the monarchy in particular  those treaties were signed with the  crown  not with any particular government with  the crown it's a special relationship a  very special relationship and now  it's him  and uh i i think  certainly he he gave me the impression  he understands that he is intensely  interested in it  and he wants to be helpful many people  say the monarchy will not be the same  without the queen  do you think  can you make the case for why  it continues to matter for canada if it  does continue to matter  well  undoubtedly  it will it will  not be the same as  the  the monarchy of elizabeth ii so when  that  powerful personality  moves aside and disappears from the  scene clearly things will change  but the  the  the issues i think canadians need to  look at is do we  do we really want to reopen  a constitutional hassle because it does  involve constitutional change is that a  productive  discussion to have  at a time where the existing apparatus  actually works pretty well  in terms of dealing with things that a  monarchy has to deal with  and if you're going to change  then  to what  what is the alternative that is going to  be  better  maybe the model in the united states  maybe not  mr goodell thank you so much pleasure  thank you  earlier today i took a walk through  green park to the mall that leads to  buckingham palace and there is a steady  stream of thousands of people many  bringing flowers even marmalade  sandwiches that's a nod to the skit the  queen did for the jubilee with  paddington bear so many people love that  there are messages like thank you for  everything rest in peace  and my favorite this card showing the  queen's corgis running from the gates of  heaven to greet her  that is global national for this sunday  i'm donna friesen thanks for watching  bye  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

